    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Prolog">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIAtr">VII Atr</ref> Prolog</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Prolog" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="260" ed="#liebermann"/>Hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VIIAtr_Prolog.lnote.oe.1"/> instituerunt Æþelredus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VIIAtr_Prolog.lnote.oe.2"/> rex<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#VIIAtr_Prolog.lnote.oe.3"/> et sapientes eius apud Badam.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#VIIAtr_Prolog.lnote.oe.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="108" ed="#robertson"/>Hoc<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#VIIAtr_Prolog.robnote.fn.3"/> instituerunt Æþelredus rex et sapientes eius apud Badam<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#VIIAtr_Prolog.robnote.fn.4"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-t"><pb n="180" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Hoc instituerunt Æþelredus rex et sapientes eius apud Badam.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="260" ed="#liebermann"/><hi rend="italic">Prolog</hi>.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VIIAtr_Prolog.lnote.de.1"/> Dies setzten König Aethelred und seine Witan zu Bath fest.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Prologue. This King Æthelred and his witan established at Bath.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="109" ed="#robertson"/>This is the edict which was drawn up by King Æthelred and his councillors at Bath<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VIIAtr_Prolog.robnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-t"><pb n="181" ed="#rabin-doml"/>King Æthelred and his councilors decreed this at Bath:</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="331"><label>close to</label> <ref target="clause:IAtr_Prolog">I Atr Prol.</ref> <quote>'Hoc instituerunt Æþelredus rex ... apud Badam' ... is not at all far from 'Ðis is seo gerædnys ... æt Wudestoce' (n. 313: VII Atr Pr., I Atr Pr.)</quote></note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">Manuscripts: Br = Johannis Brompton Chronicon (Cambridge, Corpus Christi College MS 96, and London, British Library, Cotton MS Tiberius C.xiii); Hk = Holkham 228 (privately held), fols. 82r–83v; M = Macro (privately held); T = London, British Library, Cotton MS Titus A.xxvii, fol. 145r.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">rex: omitted Br</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">Badam: habam BrHkM</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VIIAtr_Prolog.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">260</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hec <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hec Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VIIAtr_Prolog.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">260</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Eþ. <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Eþ. MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VIIAtr_Prolog.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">260</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VIIAtr_Prolog.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">260</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Habam <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Habam MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIIAtr_Prolog.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">179</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ähnlich III Atr Pro; <hi rend="italic">gerædon æt Baðan</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. Einl. 6) las wohl Q in der Agsä. Vorlage</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Similarly III Atr Pro; Q probably read <hi rend="italic">gerædon æt Baðan</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Introduction 6) in the Anglo-Saxon original</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIIAtr_Prolog.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">336</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann suggests that the incorrect reading <hi rend="italic">Habam</hi> (M, Hk, Br) may preserve the rudiments of <hi rend="italic">æt Hatum Baðum</hi> see Birch, 1257, and cf. <hi rend="italic">Hatabaðum</hi>, <hi rend="italic">Sax. Chr.</hi> ann. 972 E). He points out that in this instance the name has apparently been taken over from A.S. as in Latin it regularly appears as <hi rend="italic">Bathonia</hi> in the twelfth century, a form which was already known in the tenth (see Earle, <hi rend="italic">Land Charters</hi>, p. 375).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="VIIAtr_Prolog.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><label>Hoc</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">haec</hi> Br.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="VIIAtr_Prolog.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><label>Badam</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Habam</hi> M, Hk, Br.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
